92 0 obj
<<
/Alt (Timeline graphic of AI development from the 1980s to the 2020s. It shows four stages: Historical Foundations \(1980s-2000s\), Learning-Based Perception & Control \(2010s\), Multimodal Fusion & Reasoning \(Early 2020s\), and Cognitive Integration with Foundational Models \(Mid 2020s+\). Each stage lists key technologies and advancements, such as behavior-based systems, deep learning, multimodal reasoning, and foundational models. Notable projects like Shakey, DeepMind Atari, and OpenVLA are mentioned under each era. An arrow at the bottom represents the progression through time.)
/ID (ID.0022)
/K [676 0 R 677 0 R 678 0 R 679 0 R 680 0 R 681 0 R 682 0 R]
/P 38 0 R
/S /Figure
/T <FEFF004600690067007500720065>
/Type /StructElem
>>
endobj
93 0 obj
<<
/Alt (Diagram of a multi-layered architecture. The "Perception & Alignment Layer" includes Image, Language, and Touch Encoders, connected to FCMA and Dirichlet Confidence Fusion, outputting a Unified State Token. The "World Modeling & Structure Prediction Layer" features a World Model and Causal Graph Generator, creating a Task Graph. The "Policy Generation & Adaptation Layer" has a Prompt Encoder and Policy Decoder, producing Control Action.)
/ID (ID.0030)
/K [683 0 R 684 0 R 685 0 R 686 0 R 687 0 R 688 0 R 689 0 R]
/P 38 0 R
/S /Figure
/T <FEFF004600690067007500720065>
/Type /StructElem
>>
endobj
94 0 obj
<<
/Alt (Flowchart depicting a process from "Task Prompt" to "Unified Representation". Arrows lead from "Task Prompt" to "Feature-Conditioned Modulation", splitting into "Vision" and "Language". Both paths merge into "Structure-Aware Fusion", leading to "Unified Representation". A feedback loop labeled "Structure Feedback" connects back to "Feature-Conditioned Modulation".)
/ID (ID.0049)
/K [690 0 R 691 0 R 692 0 R 693 0 R 694 0 R 695 0 R 696 0 R]
/P 38 0 R
/S /Figure
/T <FEFF004600690067007500720065>
/Type /StructElem
>>
endobj
95 0 obj
<<
/Alt (Flowchart titled "Policy Adaptation Mechanisms" dividing into four categories: Sim2Real Transfer, Lightweight Deployment, Multi-task Policy Sharing, and Task-driven Scheduling. Sim2Real includes Domain Random, Contrastive Rep, Latent Replay. Lightweight Deployment features Prompt Compression, TinyMPC Heads, RT-2 Edge Optimized. Multi-task includes Multi-head Decoders, Shared Encoders, Prompt Routing \(ChatVLA\). Task-driven covers Lambda-based Switching, Precision-Energy Trade, DPTA Interface Control.)
/ID (ID.0087)
/K [697 0 R 698 0 R 699 0 R 700 0 R 701 0 R 702 0 R 703 0 R]
/P 38 0 R
/S /Figure
/T <FEFF004600690067007500720065>
/Type /StructElem
>>
endobj
96 0 obj
<<
/Alt (Flowchart illustrating a system pipeline. The process starts with a "Language Goal/Task Token" feeding into a "Prompt Encoder." This is followed by a "State Planner \(Plan Decoder, optional\)" connecting with a "State Token Causal Graph." The "Policy Decoder \(MPC/Transformer\)" processes information next, leading to "Control Action/Trajectory." Arrows indicate the flow of information, with interactions between steps shown through circular icons.)
/ID (ID.0097)
/K [704 0 R 705 0 R 706 0 R 707 0 R 708 0 R 709 0 R 710 0 R]
/P 38 0 R
/S /Figure
/T <FEFF004600690067007500720065>
/Type /StructElem
>>
endobj
97 0 obj
<<
/Alt (Timeline graphic titled "World Model" detailing the development stages. "Theory Foundation \(2018-2019\)" features a drawing of a person on a bicycle. "Cognitive Enhancement \(2020-2024\)" shows diagrams for World Model and Actor Critic Learning. "Unified Token \(2024-2025\)" includes images converging around the term "Gato." "Theory Reconstruction \(2025-\)" displays various graphs and diagrams. An arrow points from left to right, indicating progression. A circular label at the bottom right notes "Agent = World Model.")
/ID (ID.0111)
/K [711 0 R 252 0 R 253 0 R 712 0 R 713 0 R 201 0 R 714 0 R 202 0 R 715 0 R 716 0 R
